# Two readers of one volume at once, each its share (roadmap
# disk-scheduler.md M5, D5): init starts tests/posix/fair.c
# (TEST_POSIX_FAIR), whose two children, started together, each read C's
# NUMBERS.TXT fifteen times in calls of 1 KB. The volume's lock goes to the
# calls in the order they asked, and the disk server serves each process
# its turn: neither takes more than half as long again as the other.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_FAIR
emulators: bochs mame
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 300
---
fair: within half again of each other: yes
fair: done
